WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.720
Mind your decisions, I'm Presh Talwalkar

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:11.340
A mathematician writes numbers on a cube. On each face, the mathematician writes a positive integer.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:17.760
For clarification, a positive integer is a whole number greater than zero.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:23.220
On each vertex, the mathematician writes the product of its three adjacent faces.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.599
For example in the upper right corner

00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:32.429
The mathematician would write the number that's equal to the product of x,y,z.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.540
The mathematician does this for each of the vertices.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:43.240
If the sum of all vertices is 154, what is the sum of all faces?

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:52.400
A similar problem was asked to eighth-grade students in Taiwan, who are age roughly 13 to 14 years old.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.949
Thanks to Kieran in New Zealand for the suggestion

00:00:56.649 --> 00:01:03.448
Pause the video if you'd like to give this problem a try. And when you're ready keep watching to learn how to solve this problem

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.970
So, how can we solve this problem

00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:22.659
suppose the faces are labeled a,b,c,d,e and f

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:30.399
Suppose the face we're looking at is labeled a we'll rotate the cube to label the faces b, c and d

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.599
We'll rotate the cube again to get back to a

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.769
on the left side, we'll label it as e and we'll label the face on the right as f

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:45.759
Let's now label each vertex. This vertex will be labeled abe

00:01:47.509 --> 00:01:51.909
Then if we rotate the cube, this vertex will be labeled abf

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.759
Let's continue doing this for all the vertices

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.979
now on the bottom, we have the face d and on the left side, we have e

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:06.008
We still have d on the bottom and on the right side we have f. so we can label these two vertices

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:08.829
They will be ade and adf

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.100
Let's put these labels to the side

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:17.769
And now let's label the remaining four vertices which will be on the opposite side of the cube

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:22.420
so we'll look at face c and we'll label each of these vertices

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:28.299
On the left side will be e and on the right side will be face f

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:35.169
On the top of this will be face d. And on the bottom of c will be face b

00:02:36.019 --> 00:02:39.159
We can use these labels to label each of these vertices

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:47.380
Starting from the lower left and going clockwise. We have be, cde, cdf and cbf

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.160
We want the sum of all of the vertices

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:54.399
Let's sum the first four and the second four separately

00:02:54.920 --> 00:03:00.070
The first four we can factor out an a and the second four we can factor out a c

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:06.040
Notice the remaining bracketed terms are exactly equal in both of these equations

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:12.759
So we can further factor the sum as a + c multiplied by the bracketed term

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.709
Let's continue factoring

00:03:15.709 --> 00:03:19.238
The first two terms here have a common factor of b

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.630
The next two terms have a common factor of d

00:03:23.359 --> 00:03:26.138
We then have a common factor of e + f

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:30.940
So we get the following factorization for the sum of all these vertices

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:36.490
It'll be a + c multiplied by b + d multiplied by e + f

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.520
now recall this is equal to 154

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:48.580
since each number is a positive integer each bracketed term must be 2 or larger

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:52.340
And must be a factor of 154

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:57.400
154 factors into 2 times 7 times 11

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.960
Therefore, the three bracketed terms

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:08.580
must be equal to 2, 7 and 11, and the sum of the bracketed terms will be the sum of 2, 7 and 11

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:15.789
Therefore we have a + c plus b + d plus e + f is equal to 2 + 7 + 11

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:21.580
Now if we look at these bracketed terms, we have one of each letter

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:28.149
Therefore we have the sum of the faces and this is equal to 20 and that's the answer

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:34.329
The sum of the numbers on the faces is equal to 20. What a neat little problem

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:43.270
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube. As always, thanks for watching and thanks for your support

